---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    name: 'About Jib',
    url: `${SITE.url}/about/`,
    mainEntity: {
      '@type': 'Person',
      name: SITE.author.name,
      jobTitle: SITE.author.role,
      address: { '@type': 'PostalAddress', addressRegion: 'QLD', addressCountry: 'AU' },
      worksFor: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#org` },
    },
  },
];
---

<Page title="About Jib" description="Who builds Jib, why it exists, and how we research and check the rules in our DIY guides.">
  <h1>About Jib</h1>

  <p>Jib is built by <strong>{SITE.author.name}</strong>, an independent developer in Queensland, Australia.</p>

  <p>
    It started with a simple frustration: every home job begins with the same questions. <em>Can I do this myself? Am I even allowed to? What do I need to buy, and how much of it?</em> The answers were scattered across tradie blogs trying to sell a call-out, hardware-store guides that say “check your state’s rules”, and forum threads from 2014.
  </p>

  <p>
    Jib puts the answers in one place. Photograph a job and the app drafts the steps, the materials list and a cost range, and flags the parts that need a licensed tradie. Then it keeps every job, shopping list and before-and-after photo organised by room.
  </p>

  <h2>How we write our guides</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Official sources first.</strong> Rules about licensing and approvals come from the state regulator, the legislation or the official planning portal — and every guide lists those sources at the bottom.</li>
    <li><strong>Dated.</strong> Every guide shows the date its rules were last checked against those sources. Legal guides are re-checked regularly.</li>
    <li><strong>Honest about the limits.</strong> Where the answer is “you need a licensed tradie”, we say so plainly, even though it means you won’t do that part yourself.</li>
    <li><strong>No paid placements.</strong> No sponsored products, no affiliate links, no ads.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Spotted a mistake?</h2>
  <p>Rules change. If something on this site is out of date or wrong, please email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> with a link to the source and we’ll fix it quickly.</p>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd[0])} />
</Page>
